+**Ending**: how a run finished, written when it happens — accepted, turned down, refused to the end, done, fallen over, stopped, or overtaken. *Done* is a run with nothing to accept or turn down, which is what reading a report is. *Stopped* is a run the user replaced mid-plan with a correction or a new ask; the run that replaces it follows it in the same negotiation. *Overtaken* is a run whose plan was offered and never answered because something came first: a new ask, which follows it in the same negotiation as after a stop; a report of the workout it adapts; or the next mesocycle. A run that is waiting on an answer has no ending, and neither has one that was cut.
 
